// every country approaches the US's density of named sites (0.6 per thousand active troops).
// Not real, confirmed sites: each row says it is assessed and why. Evidence, most reliable first:
// known past garrisons (Ukraine's documented 2021 order of battle), then the military's existing
// known bases (forces stay in and around established garrison towns), then its basing patterns
// (a garrison in most provinces' main towns, dual-use airports for the air force, more forces near
// a rival's border). Sites are picked by likelihood, not by what would be optimal, at least 20 km
// apart, from OpenStreetMap towns and airports (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL).
